        "original_id": "f8e9b4e3-560a-5dd4-96b1-2a86d122fbb4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Yanzhou District, Jining, Shandong province, Shangqiu, Henan province, China\n- People: Pan Xiaoting\n- Roles: female professional pool player\n- Organizations: Women's Professional Billiard Association\n\nFacts:\n- Yanzhou, also spelled Yenchow in postal romanization, is a district and former county-level city administered by Jining in southwestern Shandong province, People's Republic of China.\n- Shangqiu, formerly romanized as Shangkiu, is a city in eastern Henan province, Central China.\n- Pan Xiaoting was born on 25 February 1982 in Yanzhou District, Jining, Shandong.\n- Pan Xiaoting is nicknamed the \"Queen of Nine-Ball\" and is sometimes referred to in Western media as Xiaoting Pan.\n- Pan Xiaoting was the first female professional pool player from China to play full-time on the Women's Professional Billiard Association tour.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fe1ab573-f377-56a2-91fc-7a18fb5f3814",
        "text": "Page: Yanzhou District. Sentence: Yanzhou (postal: Yenchow; ) is a district and former county-level city under the administration of Jining, in the southwest of Shandong province, People's Republic of China.\nPage: Shangqiu. Sentence: Shangqiu (), formerly romanized as Shangkiu, is a city in eastern Henan province, Central China.\nPage: Pan Xiaoting. Sentence: Pan Xiaoting (; born 25 February 1982 in Yanzhou District, Jining, Shandong; sometimes referred to in the Western media as Xiaoting Pan and nicknamed \"Queen of Nine-Ball\") is the first-ever female professional pool player from China to play full-time on the Women's Professional Billiard Association (WPBA) tour.",
